@startuml gonzo_stdin_plugin
hide footbox

title Stdin Plugin (Piped Input) - Why it shows "I0"

actor User
participant "stdin" as stdin
participant "Stdin Plugin" as plugin
participant "Adapter" as adapter
participant "Gonzo\nPipeline" as gonzo

== When Piping Docker Logs ==
User -> stdin: docker logs apache | gonzo
note left: Original Docker log

stdin -> plugin: Read from os.Stdin
plugin -> plugin: bufio.Scanner reads line
plugin -> plugin: Create LogEntry:\n- Source.Type = "stdin"\n- Source.Identifier = "stdin"

plugin -> adapter: LogEntry{Source: "stdin"}

adapter -> adapter: convertToJSON(LogEntry)
note right
{
  "_source": {
    "type": "stdin",
    "identifier": "stdin"
  },
  "message": "apache log line"
}
end note

adapter -> gonzo: JSON with stdin source

gonzo -> gonzo: extractSourceInfo(json)
note right: Finds _source.type="stdin"\nMaps to "I"\nID=0 (always for stdin)

gonzo -> User: Display "I0" in log view

@enduml
